// The smallest program Origin can express (ADR-0041).
//
// Four lines became three, and the one that went was the one carrying no information. The
// case is here because the *absence* of an import is the feature: a regression would look
// like a resolver error, not a wrong answer, and nothing else in the corpus would catch it
// since every other case imports `std::io` anyway.
fn main() {
    println("hello, Origin.")
    print("a")
    print("b")
    println("")
    println("\(1 + 2) items")
}
